<BaseLayout title="Differential & Axles" description="OEM Genesis Coupe diff with a billet cover and sedan axle upgrade, or the Ford 8.8 IRS swap with custom DSS axles, for LS-swapped Genesis Coupes.">
  <h1>Differential &amp; Axles</h1>
  <p>
    Two paths: keep the <strong>factory Genesis differential</strong> and upgrade the cover and axles (good to roughly 500–600 hp),
    or swap in a <strong>Ford 8.8 IRS</strong> with custom axles for big power.
  </p>

  <GuideTabs />

  <div class="tab-panel" id="oem">
  <h2 id="stock">Stock Differential</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>R-Spec cars came with a <strong>Torsen limited-slip</strong>. Other trims may be open, so check yours before building around it.</li>
    <li>2010–16 manual cars had a <strong>recall</strong> covering the rear differential and suspension crossmember bolts. Make sure it was done before adding LS torque.</li>
    <li>The stock diff and axles are the usual weak point once you add power. Plan on axles first, then an <a href="#ford-88">8.8 swap</a> for big power.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="diff-cover">Billet Diff Cover (Recommended)</h2>
  <p>
    Jason Riddle (Dream Machinez) makes a <strong>billet 6061 aluminum differential cover</strong> for the factory Genesis Coupe diff.
    It replaces the stock cast aluminum cover, adding strengthened bolt bosses and a solid side-to-side brace.
  </p>
  <p>
    It's a great piece to have no matter your power level, unless you're doing the full <a href="#ford-88">Ford 8.8 swap</a>. It's especially worth it if you're running one of the 4th-bolt diff mount kits.
  </p>
  <div class="fig-small">
    <Figure src="dmz-billet-diff-cover.png" alt="Dream Machinez billet 6061 aluminum Genesis Coupe differential cover with center brace" caption="Dream Machinez billet diff cover: finned 6061 aluminum with a solid side-to-side brace." />
  </div>
  <p>
    <a class="buy-btn" href="https://dmzrated.square.site/product/genesis-coupe-differential-cover/66" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the diff cover at Dream Machinez</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="axles">Genesis Sedan Axles (Budget Upgrade)</h2>
  <p>
    Genesis sedan axles are a cheap, easy upgrade that should carry you safely into the 500–600 hp range.
    I broke a CV joint on one at 700 hp / 650 tq on the dyno, so launching at the track might not work.
  </p>
  <div class="note"><p><strong>Important:</strong> don't order the RH/LH-<strong>TAU</strong> V8 axles. You need the <strong>-LAM</strong>.</p></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Side</th><th>Hyundai part</th><th>GSP part</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Driver (left)</td><td>49600-3M000 LH-LAM</td><td>NCV37099</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Passenger (right)</td><td>49650-3M000 RH-LAM</td><td>NCV37100</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="figs">
    <Figure src="sedan-axle-left-ncv37099.jpg" alt="GSP NCV37099 rear left CV axle listing" caption="GSP NCV37099 — driver/left." />
    <Figure src="sedan-axle-right-ncv37100.jpg" alt="GSP NCV37100 rear right CV axle listing" caption="GSP NCV37100 — passenger/right." />
    <Figure src="sedan-axle-used-left.jpg" alt="Used Genesis sedan rear left axle listing" caption="Used sedan axles are an option too." />
  </div>

  <div class="note"><p>Going past what the sedan axles can take? See the <a href="#ford-88">Ford 8.8 Swap</a> tab.</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="tab-panel" id="ford-88">
  <h2>Ford 8.8 IRS (High HP)</h2>
  <p>
    For builds targeting 1000+ hp, Jason Riddle's Ford 8.8 IRS kit is the documented path that avoids axle failures under hard launches.
    The kit replaces the stock differential and requires custom axles from The Driveshaft Shop (DSS).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>DSS axle requirements:</strong> Send your wheel hubs so DSS can broach them from 30-spline to 33-spline.
    Measure seal-to-bearing (hub) carefully:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Driver side:</strong> ~23.25&quot; (closer to 23-3/8&quot;)</li>
    <li><strong>Passenger side:</strong> ~24.25&quot; (closer to 24-3/8&quot;)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Reference order (English Rob / Robert Kapeluch, DSS invoice 114850): Side A 23.5&quot; Seal-to-BB, Side B 24.25&quot; Seal-to-BB, 108mm-30 outer CVs with GKN grease caps.
    Customer sends OEM wheel hubs to be broached to 33-spline.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Install video:</strong>
    <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/t/ZTfag4jc8/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TikTok — Ford 8.8 IRS install</a>
  </p>

